What is etcd?

It is a distrubutes reliable key-value store that is simple, secure and fast.
Traditionally DB's are in Tabular format using columns and rows. But Key-Value is different.
Whenever you need to add data to a Table in DB you ll need to insert a new column or row which might lead to have empty cells unused.
In ETCD Each entry has its own table so that the cells won't be unused.
You can take example of Employee table and watch here is you don't remember.

Example:

key: name
value: John Doe

Key: location
value: New York

key: user: John_doe
value: name=John Doe, age=45, location=NewYork

How to download ETCD?

1) Download Binaries - curl -L <Github Path> -o tar xzvf etcd-v3.3.11-linux-amd64.tar.gz
2) Extract - tar xzvf etcd-v3.3.11-linux-amd64.tar.gz
3) Run - ./etcd

Note: When we start etcd it starts with port 2379. Then you attach any client's to the etcd to store or retrieve the information.

Default client for etcd is etcdctl which is used for setting key value pairs.

Command: ./etcdctl set key1 value1
./etcdctl put key1 value1
